    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-11-23T09:20:43+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-23T09:20:43+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-22T22:50:43Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-22T22:50:43Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A trough of low pressure over the northeast will linger over the far northeast until mid week. A cold front clips the southeast today, followed by a high pressure system, which will then move across southern parts of the state on Tuesday. A trough of low pressure approaches the western border on Wednesday whilst a cold font moves over waters to the south. The trough lingers near the western border on Thursday whilst a high pressure systems moves over waters to the south.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW013" description="North West Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-11-23T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-24T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-22T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-23T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Winds southeast to southwesterly 25 to 35 km/h. Daytime maximum temperatures around 30.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">Moderate</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:00am to 5:30pm, UV Index predicted to reach 13 [Extreme]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-11-24T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-25T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-23T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-24T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers north of Marla, most likely from the late morning. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm north of Marla in the late afternoon and evening. Winds northeast to southeasterly 20 to 30 km/h tending north to northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h in the early afternoon then tending northeast to southeasterly 15 to 20 km/h in the late evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 12 and 20 with daytime temperatures reaching 28 to 33.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-11-25T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-26T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-24T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-25T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. High chance of showers west of Coober Pedy, most likely in the afternoon and evening. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm west of Coober Pedy in the afternoon and evening. Winds north to northeasterly 25 to 35 km/h turning east to southeasterly 15 to 20 km/h during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 15 and 20 with daytime temperatures reaching 30 to 36.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-11-26T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-27T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-25T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-26T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers, most likely in the morning and afternoon. The chance of a thunderstorm. Winds east to southeasterly 15 to 25 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 17 and 23 with daytime temperatures reaching the low 30s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
